WEBVTT

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:06.360
Minami?!

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.780
Yeah... When I came to, I was like this.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.690
How do you think this happened?

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.320
I don't know. Maybe it's your ability?

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.490
You do live in Sakurada, after all.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.240
Do you know what might have caused it?

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.960
I went to the haunted mountain
to look for the vampire...

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.750
But I can't remember what happened after that.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.340
Asai, you're in the Service Club, right?

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.390
I'm amazed you came here
in the middle of the night.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.020
Yeah! I don't remember anything, though!

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.520
For a ghost, you sure are cheerful.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.150
Of course! I'm a <i>ghost</i>, you know!

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.740
It's so unrealistic, and it feels special, doesn't it?!

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.200
It's Haruki. Looks like she's here.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.120
Really?! I'll go show her my ghostly self!

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:39.090
Shall I add you to my collection, too?

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.260
Are you alone?

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:46.470
Yes. Kei went on a picnic with some girl,
so I followed him here.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.680
That must be tough to deal with.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.810
It really is.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.810
We found Minami's body.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:53.860
Did she die?

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.730
She was killed.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.110
The suspect turned himself in this morning.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:01.030
His name's Yoshii Ryouji.
But he goes by "Hitsuuchi."

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:06.450
Yoshii is an absolute clean-freak,
and he can't force himself to eat anything.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:11.000
Instead, he possesses an ability that allows him
to convert information into nourishment.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:15.090
Yoshii used to suck information
directly from the person.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.500
He only took a small amount.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.260
It was enough only to leave
the person out cold for a while.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.640
That's how the rumor of the vampire came to be...

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:27.180
Yoshii created an environment
to collect information more safely.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.770
That's how the informant
known as Hitsuuchi came to be.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.730
But he ran into some trouble,
and that environment was destroyed.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:36.940
And then went back to sucking
information directly from people again.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.280
That's what happened last night.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:42.070
The victim was Minami Mirai.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:45.530
No matter how much he sucked, the amount
of information she had wouldn't diminish.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:48.160
So, Yoshii accidentally ended up sucking too much,

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.870
and Minami died along with
the information she had.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.170
<i>The ability to die while retaining information...</i>

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:58.090
<i>If you put it another way,
it's the ability to turn into a ghost.</i>

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.180
Are you going to revive her?

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.590
Yeah, I guess.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:08.220
Minami didn't seem all that sad, though.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:11.850
Actually, she seemed quite
happy over becoming a ghost.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:16.480
The truth is, it doesn't matter
what Minami is thinking.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:19.190
She was alive before the reset.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:22.860
Are you thinking about
what happened two years ago?

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:41.260
I can erase whatever I call.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.550
Right hand. Stone.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.010
Your point?

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.970
Right hand. Human body.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.810
I've decided to kill you both.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:54.140
How am I supposed to respond to such a threat?

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.310
Did you expect me to agree?

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.980
No one would accept a death threat
and let themselves get killed.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.020
Full body. Gravel.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:03.190
<i>She calls out what part of the body she wants
to activate, and then the object to erase.</i>

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.530
<i>She can reuse a body part while the call is in effect.</i>

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:09.030
<i>The new call also retains the previous call's effect.</i>

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.330
<i>She's wary of Haruki?</i>

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.170
<i>But she's only coming after me.</i>

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.430
Let's end this now.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:34.430
Murase, do you know what a MacGuffin is?

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:36.560
How do you know about that?!

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:40.570
<i>I knew it. Murase Youka and
the MacGuffin are connected.</i>

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.320
Where is the MacGuffin?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.110
Beats me. I just know its name.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.150
Very well, then.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.330
<i>Is there a time limit for the effects of her ability?</i>

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.330
Right hand. Human body.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.580
Begone!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.080
Haruki, reset!

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.710
Full body. Ability.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:58.540
Reset.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:10.430
It's July 13th. The time is 12:59:15.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.060
Looks like you reset.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.930
Was it before we went to the festival?

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.480
We still haven't gone to it yet.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.440
I'm glad to hear that.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:25.440
You liar.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:28.990
It's disappointing to hear that from a guy.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:29.820
Haruki.

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.200
Um...

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:32.950
You liar?

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.330
Hey, not bad!

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:39.000
It'd be best if you said that while scowling
at me from above a bit more, though.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.290
Kei?

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.830
You don't have to do that.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.880
You said it was a done deal, didn't you?

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.630
I don't believe I did.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:47.840
You will tomorrow.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:51.050
You think I can take responsibility
for what I said in a previous timeline?

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.100
What in the world is going on?

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:55.180
Don't worry about it.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:56.930
Even though Minami is dead?

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:00.020
She's alive... in this timeline, at least.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.520
I'll deal with Yoshii.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.940
I was nearly killed by Murase.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.940
I'll deal with that, too.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:06.980
One more thing.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.940
What is a MacGuffin?

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:13.990
A person who possesses the MacGuffin is able
to control all the special abilities in Sakurada.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.990
It's an urban legend.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:18.370
Rumors of it spread about two years ago.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.250
So it doesn't exist?

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:24.630
No. An object called "MacGuffin" does exist.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.960
It's a small black stone that's about this big.

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.420
Where is it?

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:31.800
The staff room. It's in my desk drawer.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:33.720
That concludes our discussion.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:34.890
Don't be late to class.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:39.020
I'm thinking of telling Minami about
what happened before the reset.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.520
Do whatever you want.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.360
Good morning, Kei!

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:56.830
This time, I've got a message from Friday,
July 14th, which is yesterday for you.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.700
I believe you made an important appointment—

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:07.960
Good morning.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:09.380
Morning.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.840
Nice to meet you, Murase.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.800
You don't need to keep up the act.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.600
Why are you here?

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.390
Tsushima called me here.

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.060
Do you want to kill me?

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:24.310
Why would I kill you?

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:25.810
I was just kidding.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.110
That's a sick joke.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.020
<i>She doesn't remember anything
from the previous timeline?</i>

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:32.030
By the way, are you done with saving the cat?

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:37.830
I wanted to test whether or not I could
cancel out your abilities with mine.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.160
I remember the request I made regarding the cat.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:41.870
You both aren't a threat.

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.420
<i>She remembers things from two resets ago.</i>

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:48.130
<i>That means that just the latest
reset was a reset for her.</i>

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.380
<i>Why is that?</i>

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:53.880
What do you want?

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.390
The MacGuffin was stolen.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.140
I'm gonna have you guys get it back.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.890
You were in the Service Club, too, Murase?

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.520
In name only.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:07.350
This guy has given the Bureau
the most trouble these past two years.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.320
He's your senior.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.360
Is that true?

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.440
Shouldn't we be focusing on the MacGuffin?

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.700
The thief's identity takes priority.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.910
We have a suspect.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.700
The thief is most likely Yoshii Ryouji.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.120
It's Hitsuuchi.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.580
Tell me more of what
he mentioned earlier about you.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.710
I said something selfish a long time ago. That's all.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.010
What's your objective?

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.800
We want to revive a girl.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:40.470
We're looking for an ability
that can make that happen.

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.930
I failed in the end.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.850
Are you trying to do something similar, Murase?

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:50.310
I will take down the Bureau and rebuild it.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:52.690
There are countless abilities in Sakurada.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:55.150
If they're used well, people will be even happier.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:57.990
But those in the Bureau
just observe what's going on.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.870
Asai, would you join forces with me?

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.870
Let me think about it a little.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.120
First, we need to find Hitsuuchi.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.880
That's easy.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:14.760
Right hand. What is obstructing me from Yoshii.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.050
It's this way.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.640
That's amazing. So you can even use it like that...

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:22.390
It's strange, isn't it?

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.470
This is the way to Yoshii's house.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.470
You know where it is?

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.390
Yes. I went three days ago.

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:29.850
<i>The hole in the wall...</i>

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:33.400
<i>So, it was actually a trace of
Murase searching for Hitsuuchi.</i>

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:34.980
<i>But...</i>

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.900
Hey, Kei. It's been a while.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:39.110
Or should I say, nice to meet you?

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:42.780
It's the first time I've heard
your actual voice, huh, Hitsuuchi?

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:47.290
Hey, you! I had quite an ordeal since
you disconnected my phone line!

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:50.540
It's your fault! Hand over the MacGuffin!

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.540
I can't hand over what I don't have.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.010
I'll disconnect your phone line again!

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:58.050
Wait. I'm pretty sure he's telling the truth.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:00.430
Who stole it, then?!

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.390
I don't know.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:05.560
But someone might've picked it up by chance.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:09.100
You might know that someone, Hitsuuchi.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.940
Yeah. In that case, I might know who it is.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.690
She said she'd bring the MacGuffin.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:22.530
How much of the previous timelines do you know?

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.950
Everything you told Tsushima.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:29.200
I did something really bad.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.710
Even though the reset erased everything?

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:35.460
I still did something bad.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:40.340
If you think so, then maybe you did.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:41.380
Yeah.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.090
Thanks.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:48.850
<i>That's why Hitsuuchi is still helping us despite
knowing that Minami stole the MacGuffin.</i>

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.480
Oh, you're here, too, Misora!

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.360
Are you Misora's friend?

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.650
No, I'm not.

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.360
She's Murase the Revolutionary.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:00.530
No, I'm not!

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.410
I've got something for Asai, you know.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:06.830
That means you've got the MacGuffin, huh?

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:07.910
Could you show it to me?

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.750
Here it is. It just looks like
an ordinary pebble, though.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.500
Oh, yeah? Well then, I'll take it.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:17.460
No. I promised to give it to Asai.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:19.710
It's pointless for him to have it.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.170
I think the same would apply to you.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.930
I'm special, you know.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.220
I possess an especially powerful ability.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:28.180
That doesn't matter.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.890
I've admired abilities for a long time.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:34.100
Asai is special. Misora is also special.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.190
But I can't see what's so special about you at all.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:37.610
Shut your trap!

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:38.860
I'm going to take it from you.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:39.940
Try me.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:42.240
Index fingernail. Human body.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.370
If you want to join forces, call me.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.040
You don't have to go after her.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.380
Kei...

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:00.500
This is kind of bad.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:03.420
I wanna ask you to do some work.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.720
Is it for the Service Club?

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:08.140
No, it's a request from me.

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:09.810
I've got a student that's playing hooky.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.810
Her name's Murase Youka.

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:14.060
Please brief me.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:18.770
Murase had an older brother
who was once part of the Bureau.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:22.320
He died in a car accident
in the summer of last year.

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:26.320
So, Murase thought that if the Bureau
used special abilities effectively,

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:29.990
they could've saved her brother
with someone's ability.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:34.080
She always said that she would
never forgive the Bureau.

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:37.040
Again and again and again.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:39.290
She'd just say the same thing repeatedly.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.920
Because she viewed the Bureau as her enemy,

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:47.550
you told her about the MacGuffin
to entice her to go after it.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:49.470
Yeah, that's right.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.390
Why did you approve of the request to save the cat?

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.730
I wanted you two and her to connect.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:57.190
She relies only on her ability.

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:59.900
She needs an opponent
that she'll lose to completely.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:02.690
I don't really have a way to persuade her...

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.860
Murase hurt Minami.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:06.950
It was just a scratch.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:10.780
She intentionally hurt someone using her ability.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:12.990
The Bureau will deal with it severely.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:16.500
She crossed a line that should never be crossed.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:21.790
I can only think of one method to persuade her.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:23.460
And I don't want to do that.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:33.220
Please send Murase a message.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:33.970
What should it say?

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.940
"Let's join forces and take down the Bureau.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:43.980
I'd like you to come to the Kawaharazaka's
riverside tomorrow at 11:45 a.m sharp."

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.490
Hey, what's up, Kei?

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.530
I've got a favor to ask.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.000
Hello. Would you like some?

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:00.000
There's no mayonnaise on it.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:07.420
<i>Murase probably just wanted
to get something across.</i>

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.130
<i>The same goes for Mr. Tsushima.</i>

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:12.680
<i>But that didn't go well for the two of them.</i>

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.180
I love messages.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:19.810
I want to send a lot of happy and
trivial words from person to person.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:23.020
What if it's something sad?

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:25.440
I'll figure out how to word the message.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:30.280
If it's something that should be said,
I'll use the right words to do the right thing.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:33.030
But when it gets across, the recipient will be sad.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:35.080
That's true...

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:39.370
But I believe it's still better than
the message not getting across at all.

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.620
You don't need to be afraid.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:44.250
I'm sure you'll do just fine.

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:48.550
What did you come here for?

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.340
I was thinking of climbing up a tree.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:54.180
Because I'll be doing something awful tomorrow.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:56.010
If you don't want to do it, then don't.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:59.020
I have to do it no matter what I think.

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:01.810
And to be honest, I don't really feel that guilty.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.190
And?

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:06.150
I just wanted to climb up to some high place.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.980
In order to see the distant view.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.030
You should just be honest
and say you're having a hard time.

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:13.530
I think I'm being very honest, though.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:15.700
You should tell Haruki.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.620
I'm sure she'll be happy about it.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:20.790
And she'll have a better answer for you than I do.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:23.460
The truth is, I didn't want to do that.

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:26.540
I'll bring cream puffs next time.

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:29.050
Come again sometime.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:33.050
Seeing you vulnerable is quite entertaining.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:37.050
It's not something to boast about,
but I am vulnerable for the most part.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:42.310
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:44.060
You're ten minutes early.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:45.270
Is that so?

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:48.070
I'll be honest. I ate one takoyaki.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.610
"One"? You mean, one food tray?

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.320
No, just one ball.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.780
Who ate the rest?

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.070
Nonoh did.

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:59.450
You've been spending a lot
of time with other girls lately.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:02.200
And tomorrow, I'll be seeing Murase.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:04.080
I'm going with you.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.830
Yeah. I'd be glad if you came along.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:09.090
Also, this isn't a substitute for takoyaki, but...

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:10.840
What is this?

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:18.800
How did you...

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:22.180
Uh, I mean, thank you very much.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.730
It doesn't look weird, does it?

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.690
Nah, I think it looks great.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:36.070
I've got a favor to ask for tomorrow.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:45.710
There's something I need
to ask you no matter what.

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:47.710
Did the cat really get into an accident?

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.790
Who cares about that?

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:51.630
It's important.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.760
It's more important than anything else.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:56.380
There was an accident. The cat died.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:57.840
Happy?

00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:58.800
Yes.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:03.390
I was thinking about becoming your ally.

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:04.600
Really?

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:08.100
However, let me test your ability.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:11.980
If you pass the test, I'll follow your lead.

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:16.570
But if you can't pass it,
I'll have you take down the Bureau my way.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.610
And what is this method of yours?

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:22.280
I'll have you come to school.

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:27.790
And you'll take school seriously,
graduate, then work for the Bureau.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:30.580
After that, I'll give you one suggestion
after another for the correct method,

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:31.920
and you'll change the Bureau.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:34.210
In the end, you're no different from Tsushima!

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:37.300
You're wrong. You just need to pass the test.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.800
If you make me give up with your ability, you win.

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:41.930
Let's do this, then.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:46.560
Haruki, save.

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:52.310
Save. It's July 16th, and the time is 11:48:17.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:55.070
Bang.

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:58.150
Index fingernails. Human body.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.160
Are you stupid?!

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.210
Knives are way scarier than this.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.750
Right hand. Human body.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:13.130
You'll lose your whole hand next!

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.210
That would be a problem.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:15.880
Full body. Gravel!

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:19.050
The truth is, you didn't care about our abilities.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:21.590
You just wanted us to reset to save your cat, right?

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:22.930
This has nothing to do with the cat!

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:25.180
Why did you decide to take it in, then?

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.140
Did you know that Minami Mirai died?

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.850
The girl who stole the MacGuffin?

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:35.110
She was killed by Hitsuuchi on Friday night.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.820
Who was the one who brought
the MacGuffin yesterday?

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:39.490
The same Minami.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:45.030
On Saturday at noon, we reset for the
second time after you attacked us.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.540
You had no idea, right?

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:49.330
Why would I attack you guys?

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:52.960
You wanted us to reset Minami's death.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:55.380
You thought that by attacking us,
we would reset for sure.

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:58.710
Lies! My ability can cancel out the effects of a reset!

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:01.930
If you don't wish for it, your ability won't activate.

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:04.510
You wanted a reset yourself.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:07.720
You wanted to forget Minami Mirai's death.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:10.310
I'm not that weak!

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:11.940
Full body. Human body.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:15.230
Now, you can't even touch me!

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:17.820
The same goes for you.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:19.480
If you touch me, I'll end up dead.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:21.950
I don't care what happens to you!

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:24.910
Isn't this a fight to become allies?

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.780
Enough with this! I don't need allies!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:33.920
Don't move.

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:34.920
Haruki.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:36.290
Full body. Ability.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:40.170
Don't you realize?

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.800
This is where you were standing when you saved.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:45.680
You're wrong. You're two steps off.

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:48.850
If you reset, you'll appear two steps away from me.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:51.560
I can attack you immediately after a reset!

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:54.390
I have just one thing to say.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:55.060
What is it?

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:58.980
Haruki can't reset without my orders.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:00.320
What the hell does that—

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.280
Murase...

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:04.910
It's okay to give up.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:37.400
Ding-dong-ding-dong!

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:40.400
This is a message from this morning
that will be delivered on July 16th:

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:43.860
It's the message that you've
been waiting for from Asai Kei!

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:46.530
Haruki, reset.

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:47.860
Reset.

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:56.540
Bang!

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:04.550
Sorry.

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:07.050
I don't remember anything.

00:22:07.300 --> 00:22:10.050
I know. But I'm still sorry.

00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:12.350
I give up.

00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:15.430
That cat is getting along just fine.

00:22:15.930 --> 00:22:17.810
He's taking a nap with Nonoh.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:21.520
I was happy about the request to save the cat.

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:26.320
From the bottom of my heart, I thought,
"I really want to live doing this sort of thing."

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:32.280
Savings dogs, cats, and if possible, people as well.

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:35.830
From now on, let's work toward that.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:40.920
On rainy days, let's share our umbrellas
with a person who's soaked.

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:45.050
If there's a puppy that's lost its way,
we can find its mother.

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:48.880
We can give milk to a starving cat.

00:22:49.630 --> 00:22:52.760
We can even dress up like Santa
and hand out presents for Christmas.

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:59.230
Anyway, let's just do things
that will make us smile together.

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:01.560
Yeah...

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:05.730
It'd be nice to do that.

00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:09.900
I'm sure things will go just fine,
just like it did for that cat.

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:17.200
It's okay. Enough time has already passed.

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:29.010
Congrats on your enrollment.

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:30.430
Hello. It's nice to meet you.

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:31.550
Do you like marbles?

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:33.180
It's like they're making fun of the world.

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:35.310
...said it was weird for me
to speak politely since we're classmates.

00:23:35.310 --> 00:23:36.890
Because it's something I didn't need.

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:38.310
Why are you crying?

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:39.060
I don't know!

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:48.610
We're always simply standing in a rain of eternal sadness

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:56.120
That is why I need that warmth of yours

00:23:56.700 --> 00:24:01.580
Life is but a dream we never wake up from

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:09.630
We repeat it over and over, praying for salvation

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:15.220
I kept waiting endlessly for your signal

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:22.440
To make sure you wouldn't disappear all by yourself

00:24:22.980 --> 00:24:26.940
Ah, it doesn't matter where I am or what I'm doing

00:24:26.940 --> 00:24:30.650
My heart can't go against your will

00:24:30.650 --> 00:24:36.280
So I'd follow you even to the ends of the world

00:24:36.280 --> 00:24:43.420
I fell in love with you at the dawn of our new world

00:24:43.420 --> 00:24:50.050
But we kept pushing the hand of the clock backwards

00:24:50.050 --> 00:24:57.100
And lost not only time, but our smiles as well

00:24:57.100 --> 00:25:01.180
You're the one who brought it back

00:25:01.180 --> 00:25:08.060
And taught me that even lies can be meaningful
